# Pipeline-generated deliverables/diagnostics (written by a run; not source). The
# latter also holds the command sandbox's ephemeral per-run scratch — a private
# CARGO_HOME/RUSTUP_HOME + linker TMPDIR under sandbox/ (docs/command-sandbox.md §3).
/certora/
/.certora_internal/

# Build outputs (cargo-build-sbf / crucible).
/target/
crashes/
# `Cargo.lock` is COMMITTED here, unlike the other scenarios, so this program resolves the same way
# on every machine and on any day. `cargo-build-sbf` runs the Solana platform-tools cargo (1.79),
# which parses neither an `edition2024` manifest nor a `rust-version` above its own, and a free
# resolution now picks several; the lock holds the transitive set below both boundaries.
#
# The pipeline itself survives without it — `warm_cargo_cache` fetches with a modern cargo first —
# so what the lock protects is a *direct* `cargo-build-sbf` (what anyone debugging the scenario
# reaches for) and reproducibility against registry drift, not the gate.
# Fuzzing artifacts (crucible run: corpus + explore-mode ./corpus, ./output).
/corpus/
/output/

